# direnv entry point — auto-activates the Nix devShell on `cd`.
#
# One-time setup per developer:
#   1. Install direnv (https://direnv.net) and hook it into your shell.
#   2. (Recommended) Install nix-direnv for fast, cached shell entry:
#        https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv
#   3. Run `direnv allow` in this directory once.
#
# Not using direnv? Just run `nix develop` manually — same result.
use flake

# Tell nvim's environment profile (files/nvim/lua/config/profile.lua) that
# this project provides the C/C++ and CMake toolchains — loads the clangd
# and cmake extras (LSP, DAP, formatters) only inside this shell.
# Compose-safe: keeps any host-default langs; the parser tolerates the empty
# leading token.
export NVIM_LANGS="${NVIM_LANGS:-},clang,cmake"
